---
/*
 * The story in StoryLayout (abhisekmishra.com/about's layout). Photos sit in
 * the text flow with small centred descriptions; the banner's only shows in
 * the image viewer.
 */
import StoryLayout from "@/layouts/StoryLayout.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/typography/Prose.astro";
import BlurImage from "@/components/ui/BlurImage.astro";
import hillRoad from "@/assets/bio/hill-road-dusk.jpg";
import lingeyPing from "@/assets/bio/dashain-lingey-ping.jpg";
import birthdayParty from "@/assets/bio/first-birthday-party.jpg";
import schoolUniform from "@/assets/bio/school-uniform.jpg";
import marigolds from "@/assets/bio/marigolds.jpg";
import swimmingPool from "@/assets/bio/swimming-pool.jpg";
import birthdayCake from "@/assets/bio/first-birthday-cake.jpg";

// Closing row: three photos of different shapes, cropped to one 3:4 frame
// with each crop (and its blurred preview) placed to keep the face in view
const closingPhotos = [
  {
    src: schoolUniform,
    alt: "Young Manish in a white school uniform with a striped tie and a backpack",
    position: "center top",
  },
  {
    src: marigolds,
    alt: "Young Manish in a yellow shirt making a peace sign between two men in dhaka topis, among marigolds",
    position: "center 35%",
  },
  {
    src: swimmingPool,
    alt: "Young Manish at the edge of a swimming pool, holding the tiled rim",
    position: "center 40%",
  },
];
---

<StoryLayout
  heading="Bio"
  description="A personal journal by Manish Tamang (golecodes)."
  banner={hillRoad}
  bannerAlt="Young Manish and mom standing on a dirt road in the hills of Amtek, Bhojpur, at dusk"
  bannerCaption="Me and my mom, Bhojpur, Amtek"
  bannerPosition="center 28%"
>
  <Prose class="prose-story">
    <p>
      <span class="lead"
        >Since childhood, I have been driven by curiosity and a deep passion
        for learning :)</span
      >
      I have always been eager to explore new ideas and understand how things
      work, often looking at them from different perspectives.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am naturally drawn to minimalism and clarity, preferring simplicity
      over anything cluttered or messy. From the very beginning, I have
      carried a positive mindset toward growth, always seeking to learn,
      improve, and see the bigger picture.
    </p>
    <p>
      I was born in Bhojpur, Nepal, in 2008. I moved to Itahari for school,
      then to Kathmandu after the 6th grade, and later back to Itahari for my
      +2. Now I'm in Kathmandu again, working on small client projects,
      freelancing, and trying to figure out the next few years.
    </p>

    <figure>
      <BlurImage
        src={lingeyPing}
        alt="Young Manish smiling while swinging on a tall bamboo and rope swing in a hillside field"
        widths={[592, 1184, 1500]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 592px"
        quality={78}
        data-zoom
      />
      <figcaption>Mini me enjoying lingey ping (swing) on Dashain. Pic: my mama, Bijay Moktan</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      In the 6th grade I saw QBasic on a projector for the first time, and
      that was it. I knew I wanted to go toward computers. In 7th and 8th
      grade, my computer teacher, Nishan sir, made the basics feel easy, and I
      loved solving QBasic problems.
    </p>
    <p>
      My web journey started in 9th grade, around 2021–2022. My new computer
      teacher at Prashanti Academy, Millan Sunuwar Rawacha sir (<a
        href="https://www.youtube.com/@millan.977">his YouTube channel</a
      >), saw some potential in me and asked, why not build a website for the
      school? I said, why not, I can do anything.
    </p>
    <p>
      I went home to my brother's Acer laptop. All I knew was that a website
      is a collection of web pages, and I only knew how to make one in
      Notepad. I never thought about hosting. A few days later I showed him my
      page on a pen drive. He liked it, but said it wasn't a real task yet:
      now host it and make it public.
    </p>
    <p>
      I had no idea what that meant, so I did some research, found Netlify,
      and put my first site online under my own name at <a
        href="https://manishtamang.netlify.app/">manishtamang.netlify.app</a
      >. More of that time is in <a
        href="/blog/my-personal-journey-with-prashanti-academy-a-tale-of-growth-and-gratitude"
        >my Prashanti Academy post</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      After that I wanted to build dynamic sites. I spent almost six months
      on PHP because it was trending, then found Next.js and left PHP behind.
      I still couldn't make a properly dynamic site, until I learned about
      CMSs and started building with Sanity. They even sent me some merch: a
      t-shirt in 2023 and a sweatshirt in 2024.
    </p>

    <!-- Two 3:4 photos side by side under one description; the viewer shows it for both -->
    <figure>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <BlurImage
          src={birthdayParty}
          alt="Three kids in party hats sitting behind a table with a lit birthday cake"
          widths={[290, 580, 768]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 50vw, 290px"
          quality={78}
          data-zoom
          class="aspect-3/4 w-full object-cover"
        />
        <BlurImage
          src={birthdayCake}
          alt="A birthday cake with pink icing roses that reads Happy Birthday Manish Tamang"
          widths={[290, 580, 768]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 50vw, 290px"
          quality={78}
          data-zoom
          class="aspect-3/4 w-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>My first ever birthday cake celebration</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      The journey is still going. I make minimal sites, freelance, and build
      projects. I've earned a bit along the way, and I'm still learning and
      working out what I'm for, and what's next.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      {closingPhotos.map(({ src, alt, position }) => (
        <BlurImage
          src={src}
          alt={alt}
          widths={[190, 380, 570]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 31vw, 190px"
          quality={78}
          data-zoom
          position={position}
          class="aspect-3/4 w-full object-cover"
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  </Prose>
</StoryLayout>
